{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789789537,"nonce":"LBjW+0RAg73mwadHxvEZ2JTh+b0=","title":"Python: a dict lookup that raised was then read as its value type","message":"`d[k]` and `d.pop(k)` on a dict of known value type coerced the fallible\nlookup's result straight to the value kind, `zb_any_as_i64(zb_dict_get(d, k))`.\nA missing key left a KeyError pending and returned null, and the coercion\nthen raised TypeError (\"'NoneType' object cannot be interpreted as an\ninteger\") before any pending check ran, so `except KeyError` never caught it\n(conformance exceptions/raised_in_loop, dict/string_keys).\n\nFix: `read_as` checks a fallible call before reading its value as the\nshape says; the coercion's own check follows.","files":null}]}